<div class="tw-p-2 tw-font-alt">
    {{!-- Trained / Basic skills flow into 1–3 width-responsive columns (#267).
         auto-fit makes the grid track count follow the PANEL width (not the
         viewport): it collapses to a single column on a narrow sheet and caps
         at three via the max(min-col, container/3) idiom (gap = 0.5rem ⇒ two
         gaps subtracted at the 3-column breakpoint).

         Floor is 20rem, DERIVED rather than tuned (#267). The floor had been
         ping-ponged 14rem → 10rem chasing symptoms, but a skill row's fixed chrome
         alone is ~252px on the 4-pip lines (DH2e/BC/OW): 16px row padding + 2px
         border + 16px grid gaps + 40px score track + 108px indicator strip
         (4 × 24px pips + gaps/padding/border) + 16px icon + 14px inner gaps +
         ~40px for the dice and favourite buttons. Both previous floors sat BELOW
         that, so the floor never bound: auto-fit always fitted three columns and
         the name cell was allocated less than zero space, which is why names
         clipped and the row never reflowed. 20rem (320px) = that chrome plus
         ~68px of readable name, so auto-fit now genuinely drops 3 → 2 → 1 as the
         panel narrows. Pairs with tw-shrink-0 on the row's trailing buttons.
         Skills render from the flat `standard` list in row-major order rather
         than the old fixed two-array column split. --}}
    <div class="tw-grid tw-gap-2 tw-relative" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(max(20rem, calc((100% - 1rem) / 3)), 1fr));">
        {{#each skillLists.standard as |entry|}}
            {{> systems/wh40k-rpg/templates/actor/partial/skill-row.hbs entry=entry}}
        {{/each}}
    </div>

    {{!-- DH2e has no separate "Advanced Skills" tier; advancedUntrained is now empty and
         every standard skill renders in the responsive grid above. See issue #2. --}}
</div>
